# Findings of `make azure-platform-scan` that are accepted for this module (S020).
# None: on the pinned image the module has no HIGH or CRITICAL finding, so this
# file holds no entry. The module is written, checked and never planned or
# applied; nothing is hidden here: its MEDIUM and LOW findings are reported for
# the module's README, which the step's documents contract writes.
#
# An entry would be one Trivy check ID per line, exactly `AZU-` and four digits
# and nothing after it (no expiry, no file name, no wildcard, not the older
# AVD- spelling), and on the line directly above it the reason: what the check
# says, why it holds here, and what a production environment would do instead,
# in a handful of words at least. tests/meridian/test_azure_scan.py fails on an
# entry that breaks any of this, on an entry at all that its list does not name,
# on an inline ignore comment in a .tf file, on a Trivy configuration or YAML
# ignore file in this directory, and on a change in the number of cluster,
# registry, database server or subnet blocks: an entry here applies to EVERY
# resource of the directory, not to one. A finding fixed in the module is deleted
# from here.
